==============================================================================
SYSMON XML FIELD EXTRACTION (rex-based)
==============================================================================
Use these patterns when the Splunk Add-on for Microsoft Sysmon is NOT installed.
The regex extractions pull fields directly from the raw XML.

If you DO have the add-on installed, fields auto-extract and these aren't
needed — but they still work as a fallback.
==============================================================================


==============================================================================
BASE TEMPLATE: Extract all common Sysmon fields
==============================================================================
Copy this as the starting point for any Sysmon-based detection.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ParentImage'>(?<ParentImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ParentCommandLine'>(?<ParentCommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='User'>(?<User>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ProcessId'>(?<ProcessId>\d+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ProcessGuid'>(?<ProcessGuid>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Hashes'>(?<Hashes>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, EventID, Image, CommandLine, ParentImage, User


==============================================================================
EVENT ID 1: Process Creation
==============================================================================
Most important event for attack detection. Use this template:

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=1
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ParentImage'>(?<ParentImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='User'>(?<User>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, User, Image, CommandLine, ParentImage
| sort -_time


==============================================================================
EVENT ID 3: Network Connection
==============================================================================
Tracks outbound connections from processes. Critical for C2 detection.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=3
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='SourceIp'>(?<SourceIp>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='DestinationIp'>(?<DestinationIp>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='DestinationPort'>(?<DestinationPort>\d+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='DestinationHostname'>(?<DestinationHostname>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, Image, SourceIp, DestinationIp, DestinationPort, DestinationHostname


==============================================================================
EVENT ID 10: Process Access (LSASS Dumping Indicator)
==============================================================================
When a process accesses another process's memory. Used to detect Mimikatz.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=10
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='SourceImage'>(?<SourceImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetImage'>(?<TargetImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='GrantedAccess'>(?<GrantedAccess>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, SourceImage, TargetImage, GrantedAccess


==============================================================================
EVENT ID 11: File Creation
==============================================================================
Tracks file creation - useful for staging, dropper detection.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=11
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetFilename'>(?<TargetFilename>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, Image, TargetFilename


==============================================================================
EVENT ID 13: Registry Value Set
==============================================================================
Persistence detection - autoruns, services, etc.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=13
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetObject'>(?<TargetObject>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Details'>(?<Details>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, Image, TargetObject, Details


==============================================================================
EVENT ID 22: DNS Query
==============================================================================
Catches DNS-based C2 indicators.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=22
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='QueryName'>(?<QueryName>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='QueryResults'>(?<QueryResults>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, Image, QueryName, QueryResults
